  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Emergency Health Response and Humanitarian Border Management in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the armed conflict that suddenly erupted in Sudan on 15 April 2023 that has so far displaced more than six million people, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) through this project aims to improve basic service provision of lifesaving humanitarian assistance at the main points of entry (PoEs) in Sudan, namely Ashkeet PoE in Northern state and Galabat PoE in Gedaref state. This is achieved through a two-pronged approach consisting of improving the existing primary healthcare centers at both PoEs with integrated service of health, nutrition, mental health and psychosocial support, and protection services; strengthening capacity of frontline workers in humanitarian border management; and constructing a covered waiting area for vulnerable individuals at Ashkeet PoE.</narrative>
  </description>
